----------------------- MODULE StepwiseRefObl -----------------------
(***************************************************************************)
(* Obligations for `stepwise`. Variable-free, like every obligations        *)
(* module: each operator takes observation records and mentions no state    *)
(* variable, which is what lets harness/grade.sh EXTEND it beside a         *)
(* submission whose variables are its own business.                         *)
(*                                                                          *)
(* NAMES IN THIS FILE ARE NEVER EMITTED. Every obligation is reported under *)
(* an opaque digest, and a step obligation gets the same `R-` prefix a      *)
(* one-state conjunct gets -- which of a problem's requirements are about   *)
(* transitions is part of the decomposition, and the decomposition is what  *)
(* V2-PLAN.md 6b.2 protects.                                                *)
(***************************************************************************)
EXTENDS Naturals, Integers

(***************************************************************************)
(* THE DECLARED OBSERVATION DOMAIN: the records the observation may take.   *)
(*                                                                          *)
(* grade.sh generates a chaos submission over this and refuses the package  *)
(* if every obligation below is true of it. That is the whole reason this   *)
(* package exists, read from the reference side rather than the submission  *)
(* side: `chaos-observations` is the same spec by hand, and Step_onestep is *)
(* what refuses both. Bead tla-x8s.                                         *)
(***************************************************************************)
ObsDomain == [level: 0..3]

(***************************************************************************)
(* PHI_1 -- the box holds between zero and three parcels. A one-state       *)
(* predicate, and everything the grading engine could express before.       *)
(***************************************************************************)
Req_capacity(o) == o.level \in 0..3

(***************************************************************************)
(* PHI_2 -- one parcel at a time. TWO STATES: `o` is the current            *)
(* observation and `p` the next.                                            *)
(*                                                                          *)
(* THIS HAS NO INVARIANT FORM under this observation record, and that is    *)
(* the point of the fixture rather than an accident of how it is written.   *)
(* "One at a time" is a fact about a transition, and no predicate over a    *)
(* single observation can constrain a transition relation. A spec that is   *)
(* pure chaos over 0..3 satisfies every single-state requirement a          *)
(* reference can state about this system while having no transition         *)
(* structure whatsoever -- see the `chaos-observations` submission, which   *)
(* graded a clean PASS against the state-only `lockbox` reference as it     *)
(* stood before bead tla-x8s repaired that reference.                       *)
(*                                                                          *)
(* grade.sh judges this as [][Step_onestep(Observe, Observe')]_Observe,     *)
(* declared PROPERTY. The subscript is Observe rather than vars on purpose: *)
(* a step that moves a submission's internal state without moving the       *)
(* observation is a stutter on the observation, so a learner who splits     *)
(* their steps more finely than this reference does is not penalised for    *)
(* it. Representation is theirs (3.2); grading keys off the observation     *)
(* (3.3).                                                                   *)
(***************************************************************************)
Step_onestep(o, p) == p.level - o.level \in {-1, 0, 1}

(***************************************************************************)
(* TWO LANDMARKS, AND THE SECOND ONE IS LOAD-BEARING RATHER THAN THOROUGH.  *)
(*                                                                          *)
(* [][A]_Observe unfolds to `A \/ UNCHANGED Observe`, so a submission whose *)
(* observation operator never moves satisfies the step obligation above     *)
(* vacuously, at rc=0 -- the frozen-mapping trapdoor from the TLAiBench     *)
(* survey 6, reappearing inside the fix for it. Nothing written inside      *)
(* Step_onestep can close that, because Step_onestep is never the disjunct  *)
(* that gets taken.                                                         *)
(*                                                                          *)
(* The landmark suite closes it. A frozen observation is ONE value, and one *)
(* value cannot be both 3 and 0. grade.sh REQUIRES this of any obligations  *)
(* module that states a Step_* -- two or more landmarks, pairwise           *)
(* unsatisfiable -- and refuses the problem package otherwise, rather than  *)
(* leaving it as advice in a header. See the `frozen-observe` submission,   *)
(* which passes the step obligation and is caught here.                     *)
(***************************************************************************)
Landmark_full(o)  == o.level = 3
Landmark_empty(o) == o.level = 0

=============================================================================
